# Docker build prerequisites that must be (re)generated locally before
# `docker build`, rather than committed:
#
# - docker/Miniconda3.sh   : fetch with
#     curl -o docker/Miniconda3.sh https://repo.anaconda.com/miniconda/Miniconda3-latest-Linux-x86_64.sh
#   (sha256 of the exact file used for the recorded build is pinned in
#   ENVIRONMENT.lock)
#
# - docker/sigma-src/      : SigMA (github.com/parklab/SigMA) is licensed
#   "Academic and Non-Commercial Research Use" with an explicit
#   NO-REDISTRIBUTION clause (see its LICENSE file once cloned), so its
#   source may not be published/pushed into this repository. Fetch the
#   pinned commit locally before building:
#     git clone https://github.com/parklab/sigma docker/sigma-src
#     git -C docker/sigma-src checkout <commit recorded in ENVIRONMENT.lock>
#     rm -rf docker/sigma-src/.git
#
# - docker/agent-proxy-ca.crt : this session's network-egress-proxy CA
#   certificate, needed only to build inside this sandboxed environment's
#   TLS-inspecting proxy. Not meaningful outside it; a rebuild on an
#   unrestricted network can drop the COPY/update-ca-certificates step in
#   docker/Dockerfile entirely.
docker/Miniconda3.sh
docker/sigma-src/
docker/agent-proxy-ca.crt

__pycache__/
*.pyc
